ll retire later this year following clashes with the White House.Why it matters:Bunch's departure leaves the Smithsonian facing a leadership transition as theTrumpadministration escalates efforts to reshape how the institution presents American history.Driving the news:Bunch will step down by the end of the year after nearly 38 years at the Smithsonian, the institution said Tuesday.\"It is time for my next chapter, a chapter that will allow me to continue to protect the integrity of the Smithsonian and to champion the importance of a history that illuminates and celebrates the complex story of our nation,\" Bunch said.Flashback:Bunch pushed back against a White House review of the Smithsonian in a July message to staff, saying the report was \"not a fair characterization\" of the National Museum of American History.He said the Smithsonian remained committed to \"scholarship, nonpartisanship, independence, accuracy, and integrity.\"What's ne...", "published_at": "2026-09-08T16:47:12+00:00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Axios", "tier": "us_major", "url": "https://www.axios.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 35, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 12, "confidence": 0.29, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 11.1, "keyword_emphasis_score": 0.0, "omission_score": 38.7, "headline_body_divergence": 15.1, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}, {"article": {"id": "71b974a2-b122-45fd-a3da-1468aea5b18e", "title": "Smithsonian Secretary Lonnie Bunch to Step Down", "url": "https://www.dailysignal.com/2026/09/08/smithsonian-secretary-lonnie-bunch-to-step-down/", "summary": "The secretary of the Smithsonian Institution, Lonnie G. Bunch III, is stepping down, amid continued criticism from the White House about the direction of the Smithsonian museums. &#8220;There is no place like the Smithsonian—it has been one of the great loves of my life, and I am extraordinarily proud of what we have accomplished together,&#8221;..."